1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,980
This man turned a five hundred dollar loan into almost two thousand.

2
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:08,000
Who is he? Scott Tucker, who ran online payday loans.

3
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:11,960
What's a payday loan? A small loan you pay back on your next payday.

4
00:00:12,520 --> 00:00:16,000
His paperwork promised this: borrow five hundred, pay back six hundred fifty.

5
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:21,440
Here's the trick. The loan renewed by itself, every single payday.

6
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:24,920
Each time, his company took a hundred fifty dollars in fees.

7
00:00:25,340 --> 00:00:27,260
Hit like if you've ever signed without reading.

8
00:00:27,260 --> 00:00:30,240
But the five hundred you borrowed? It never went down.

9
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:33,340
It's like paying rent on your own debt, every two weeks.

10
00:00:33,860 --> 00:00:38,520
The Justice Department says one borrower paid nineteen hundred twenty-five dollars on that loan.

11
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:42,160
Prosecutors said the rates hit around seven hundred percent a year.

12
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:45,180
Send this to the friend who says it's just a small fee.

13
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:48,580
It wasn't one borrower, it was at least four and a half million.

14
00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:51,360
His business made over three and a half billion dollars.

15
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:56,400
So where did the money go? Some of it paid for his own professional race car team.

16
00:00:56,400 --> 00:01:00,940
Then states tried to stop him, so he claimed Native American tribes owned the business.

17
00:01:01,440 --> 00:01:03,160
Why? States can't sue tribes.

18
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:05,380
But prosecutors called that a sham.

19
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:08,100
Follow if you like seeing the math catch the bad guy.

20
00:01:08,580 --> 00:01:13,820
In twenty sixteen, he was arrested. A year later, a jury convicted him on all fourteen counts.

21
00:01:14,260 --> 00:01:17,980
He was sentenced to two hundred months in prison, more than sixteen years.

22
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:22,420
Five hundred borrowed, almost two thousand paid. Would you have read the fine print?

